-- title:
--   Filtered lifts preserve finite generation
-- statement:
--   If the polynomial ring is finite over the algebra generated by the exact degree-D weighted components, and every supported term of each original generator has weighted degree at most D, then the polynomial ring is finite over the algebra generated by the original generators.
-- source:
--   openai/math Ampleness stack: WeightedIdealCurveBound implies eps-ample exceptional twist, hence Serre vanishing and eventual generation of I^n by weight ≤ n(rho+eps) sections.

